<title>FRANCE: EU grants free-mkt soft wheat, barley.</title>
<headline>EU grants free-mkt soft wheat, barley.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following rebates to export free-market grain to non-EU countries, grain traders said.</p>
<p>			 Tonnage		Maximum rebate</p>
<p> Soft wheat	  260,000		14.67 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Barley		140,000		28.99 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Oats		  33,000		 34.70 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Durum		 19,800		  6.98 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Greek maize				  Rejected</p>
<p> Oats to Switzerland/Liechtenstein    Rejected</p>
<p> Rye		   10,000		 31.45 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>EU member country officials later confirmed these figures.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
</text>
